\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Right-scalar columns for a symmetry selector}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Use the [right-scalar column coordinates](fdip-0050). For
#{D_\Xi=\operatorname{End}_\Gamma(W_\Xi)} and
#{r_\Xi=\dim_{D_\Xi}W_\Xi}, represent #{H_\Xi} by #{r_\Xi}
columns in #{D_\Xi^{m_\Xi}}. Matrices act on each column by left
multiplication. A subrepresentation #{X} meets the isotypic
component in
##{X\cap H_\Xi
 \cong\{(z_1,\ldots,z_{r_\Xi}):z_a\in U_\Xi\}}
for a right #{D_\Xi}-subspace
#{U_\Xi\subseteq D_\Xi^{m_\Xi}}. Postcomposition by #{Q} is left
multiplication by the Hermitian matrix #{Q_\Xi} on every column.
The invariance #{Q\cdot M_\Xi(X)\subseteq M_\Xi(X)} of
\ref{fdip-005N} is exactly #{Q_\Xi U_\Xi\subseteq U_\Xi}. A right
#{D_\Xi}-basis of eigenvectors of #{Q\cdot} is a
#{D_\Xi}-basis of #{U_\Xi} consisting of #{Q_\Xi}-eigenvectors.
Repeated eigenvalues still allow a proper subspace of one
eigenspace.}
